# transparency, not in translator-credits.
#
# Glossary (follow Bokmålsordboka, https://ordbokene.no):
#   scan (verb) = skanne, imperative «skann», past «skannet»
#   scan (the act) = skanning; never write «scan» in Norwegian text
#   scanner (program) = skanner, e.g. «virusskanner»
#   threat = trussel; infected = infisert
#   quarantine = karantene; quarantined = satt i karantene
#   virus definitions = virusdefinisjoner; signatures = signaturer
#   daemon (clamd) = tjeneste; «clamd-tjenesten» / «freshclam-tjenesten» if ambiguous
#   rate limited (freshclam cool-down) = midlertidig begrenset;
#     the cause = repetisjonsbegrensning; VirusTotal rate limit = hastighetsgrense
#   on-access scanning = sanntidsskanning; scheduled scan = planlagt skanning
#   exclusions = unntak
#   mirror / CDN = nedlastingsserver (plain language, not «speil»/«CDN»)
#   folder / directory = mappe, also in technical contexts (DatabaseDirectory);
#     users don't relate to «katalog»
#   Preferences (the app window, per-user) = Brukervalg
#   settings (ClamAV/system configuration) = innstillinger
#   tray / system tray / notification area = varslingsområde (Språkrådet, Microsoft)
#   privileged helper = privilegert hjelper
#   Save & Apply = Lagre og bruk
#
# Tools named in the strings (never translate the names):
#   ClamAV           the antivirus engine and project as a whole
#   clamscan         scanner the user starts; loads the database on every run
#   clamd            ClamAV daemon; keeps the database in memory. Follow the
#                    source's name: "ClamAV daemon" = «ClamAV-tjenesten»,
#                    "clamd daemon" = «clamd-tjenesten»; package clamav-daemon (Debian),
#                    unit clamd@scan (Fedora)
#   clamdscan        client that asks clamd to scan; needs clamd running
#   clamonacc        on-access (sanntids) scanning client, works with clamd
#   freshclam        downloads/updates the virus database; service
#                    clamav-freshclam (Debian) or freshclam
#   fangfrisch, clamav-unofficial-sigs
#                    third-party tools that fetch extra signature databases
#   Lynis            security audit (revisjon) tool; chkrootkit: rootkit scanner
#   pkexec / polkit  ask for administrator rights («administratortilgang»)
#   flatpak-spawn    runs host commands from inside the Flatpak sandbox
#
# Style: sentence case, not English Title Case («Skanning fullført»).
# Counts in pseudo-plurals like "threat(s)": always keep what is counted.
# Mirror the source with «(er)» («{count} trussel(er)», «{count} fil(er)»),
# or use number-neutral wording that still names it («{count} av filene»).
# Never drop the noun («{count} funn», «{count} stk.») and never use
# «trusler oppdaget: {count}».
# Dashes: spaced en dash « – » as tankestrek; en dash without spaces in
# ranges («1–28»). Quotation marks: «…».
# Number + unit: never a plain space, so the pair can't break across lines.
#   unit symbols (s, min, t, kB, MB, %, d.): U+202F NARROW NO-BREAK SPACE
#   whole words (sekunder, minutter, dager, byte, …): U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE
# Both are invisible in most editors; check with e.g. `grep -P '\x{202F}'`.
#
